{"id":"word:hebrew:H5060","type":"word","title":"נָגַע","subtitle":"H5060 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to touch , i.e. lay the hand upon (for any purpose; euphemistically, to lie with a woman); by implication, to reach (figuratively, to arrive , acquire ); violently, to strike (punish, defeat, destroy, etc.)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָגַע (H5060) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 150 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָגַע (nâgaʻ) means properly, to touch , i.e. lay the hand upon (for any purpose; euphemistically, to lie with a woman); by implication, to reach (figuratively, to arrive , acquire ); violently, to strike (punish, defeat, destroy, etc.) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 16 22."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָגַע","transliteration":"nâgaʻ","pronunciation":"naw-gah'","strong":"H5060","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5060","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["הַ/נֹּגֵ֥עַ","נֹגֵ֣עַ","נָ֣גְעָה","וַ/יִּגַּע֙","יִגַּ֖ע"],"morphs":[["HTd/Vqrmsa",20],["HVqi3ms",14],["HC/Vqw3ms",10],["HVhrmsa",7],["HVhp3ms",7],["HVqrmsa",6],["HVqp3ms",6],["HVqi3fs",6],["HVqj2mp",5],["HR/Vqc",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to touch , i.e. lay the hand upon (for any purpose; euphemistically, to lie with a woman); by implication, to reach (figuratively, to arrive , acquire ); violently, to strike (punish, defeat, destroy, etc.)","usage":"beat, (× be able to) bring (down), cast, come (nigh), draw near (nigh), get up, happen, join, near, plague, reach (up), smite, strike, touch.","full":"H5060. naga נָגַע :150 verb touch, reach, strike (Late Hebrew id. ; Arabic is agree with one (of food), produce effect ; Aramaic נְגַע Ithpa`al be struck (that is, with leprosy), compare Pi`el below); — Qal Perfect ׳נ Genesis 32:33 +; נָָֽגְעָה Judg 20:41 +; 1 plural suffix נְנַעֲנוּךָ Gen 26:29 ; Imperfect יִגַּע Lev 5:3 +; וַיִּגַּע Gen 32:26 +, etc.; Imperative גַּע Psa 144:5 2 t.; Infinitive construct לִנְגּוֺעַ נְגֹעַ, Gen 20:6 3 t.; גַּ֫עַת 2Sam 14:10 ; Ezek 17:10 ; suffix נָגְעֵךְ Ruth 2:9 etc.; Participle active נֹגֵעַ 1Kin 19:5 +; נֹגְעִים Jer 12:14 ; feminine נֹגַ֫עַת Num 19:22 2 t.; plural נֹגְעֹת 1Kin 6:27 ; passive נָגוּעַ Psa 73:14 ; Isa 53:4 ; &#8212; 1. a. touch , usually followed by בְּ Gen 3:3 (J), 32:25 ; Genesis 32:33; Exod 19:12 (twice in verse); 19:13 (all E), 29:37 ; 30:20 (P), Lev 5:2 , 325t. Leviticus; Num 16:26 7 t. Numbers (P) + 19:22 (no בְּ or object), Deut 14:8 ; Judg 6:21 ; 2Sam 23:7 ; 1Kin 6:27 (twice in verse); 19:5 , 7 ; 2Kin 13:21 ; Est 5:2 ; Dan 8:5 , 18 ; Lam 4:14 ; followed by אֶלֿ Hag 2:12 ; Num 4:15 ; 1Kin 6:27 ; Dan 9:21 , compare Hosea 4:2 ; compare עַלמֶּֿה Isa 6:7 ; עַלשָֿׂפָה Dan 10:16 ; compare accusative Isa 52:11 ; absolute (no object expressed) Job 6:7 ; Lam 4:15 . b. of ׳י touching earth, mountains, etc., followed by בְּ Amos 9:5 ; Psa 104:32 ; 144:5 ; figurative of ׳י touching the heart, followed by בְּ 1Sam 10:26 . 2 nearly = strike , passive stricken , Psa 73:14 ; Isa 53:4 || מֻכֶּה ), of wind Job 1:19 ; Ezek 17:10 ; of divine chastisement 1Sam 6:9 ; Job 1:11 ; 19:21 ; followed by אֶל 2:5 . 3 touch = harm, followed by. בְּ , Gen 26:11 (J), Josh 9:19 ; 2Sam 14:10 ; 1Chr 16:22 || הָרֵעַ ) = Psa 105:15 ; Jer 12:14 ; Zech 2:12 (twice in verse); followed by. אֶלֿ Gen 20:6 ( touch a woman), so Prov 6:29 (followed by בְּ ); followed by. accusative Gen 26:29 (J, suffix), so Ruth 2:9 ; see also Job 5:19 (subject רַע , followed by בְּ ), Judg 20:34 , 41 (both subject רָעָה , followed by עַלֿ ). 4 reach, extend to , 2Sam 5:8 , followed by בְּ (but corrupt see Dr HPS); in metaphor, followed by עַד , of vine Isa 16:8 ; Jer 48:32 ; of sword 4:10 , compare 4:18 ; of chastisement Micah 1:9 , compare Job 4:5 (|| אֶלֿ בּוֺא ); also (followed by אֶל ) Jer 51:9 ; = come , followed by אֶלֿ Jonah 3:6 ; arrive (of time), absolute Ezra 3:1 ; Neh 7:73 . Niph`al Imperfect וַיִּנָָּֽנְעוּ Josh 8:15 be stricken, defeated (in battle), i.e. feign to be so, but read probably וַיִּנָָּֽגְפוּ , see נגף Niph`al Pi`el Perfect suffix נִגְּעוֺ 2Chr 26:20 strike (with leprosy, 2 accusative), subject ׳י ; so Imperfect וַיְנַגַּע 2Kin 15:5 ; Gen 12:17 (subject ׳י ; accusative of person + accusative of cognate meaning). Pu`al Imperfect יְנֻגָּע֑וּ be sticken by diseases (?; compare Pi`el and נֶגַע 2. 3. especially 2Sam 7:14 ) Psa 73:5 . Hiph`il Perfect הִגִּיעַ Isa 25:12 6 t.; 2 feminine singular הִגַּ֫עַתְּ Est 4:14 ; 1 singular suffix וְהִגַּעְתִּ֫יהוּ Ezek 13:14 , etc.; Imperfect יַגִּיעַ Isa 8:8 3 t.; וַיַּגַּע 6:7 ; Jer 1:9 , etc.; Infinitive construct הַגִּיעַ Est 2:12 , 15 ; Participle מַגִּיעַ Gen 28:12 +; feminine מַגַּ֫עַת 2Chr 3:11 ; — cause to touch; reach, approach, arrive: 1 cause to touch, apply , Exod 12:22 ) (J E; אֶלֿ מִדָּם, ); cause to touch (compare לָאָרֶץ עָפָר, עַד ), i.e. bring to ground, Isa 25:5 , 12 , compare Lam 2:2 ; Ezek 13:14 (followed by אֶלֿ ), Exod 4:25 (J; followed by לְרַגְלָיו ); followed by עַלמֶּֿה Isa 6:7 ; Jer 1:9 ; followed by בְּ Isa 5:8 . 2 intransitive reach, extend , Gen 28:12 (followed by ָ ה locative); followed by אֶלֿ Zech 14:5 , followed by עַד Isa 8:8 ; compare שֶׂה דֵּי יָדוֺ ׳תַּגּ Lev 5:7 if his hand do not reach enough for a lamb (i.e. he be not able to furnish a lamb); followed by לְ Job 20:6 (hyperbole) 2Chr 3:11 (twice in verse); 3:12 ; followed by לְ עַד 28:9 ; attain , followed by לְ Est 4:14 , arrive, come , followed by accusative of location Isa 30:4 ; Est 4:3 ; 8:17 , followed by לְ (of time) Dan 12:12 , followed by אֶלֿ 1Sam 14:9 , followed by עַדֿ Psa 107:18 , absolute Est 6:14 ; followed by אֵצֶל Dan 8:7 . 3 approach , of time, absolute Eccl 12:1 ; Song 2:12 ; Ezek 7:12 (|| בּוֺא ); see also Est 9:1 (followed by Infinitive), compare 2:12 , 15 ; Psa 88:4 (followed by לְ ). 4 of fate or lot, = befal , followed by אֶלֿ Est 9:26 ; Eccl 8:14 (twice in verse); Psa 32:6 .","rootNote":